---
description: Keep every player-facing string localizable and the English template in sync
alwaysApply: true
---

# Localization

Translators work from `ModuleData/Languages/pfx_strings_en.xml`. A string without an id, or missing
from that file, stays English in every language.

- **Every player-facing string gets an id**: perk and skill-effect descriptions, `TextObject` text,
  MCM setting names, `HintText`, and group names. Form: `"{=PFx_Name}English text"`. Log and
  `Debug.Print` text needs none.
- **Id names**: perk text `PFx_<Perk>` (variants get a suffix, e.g. `PFx_FootworkNoShield`);
  MCM `PFx_Mcm_<PropertyName>` and `PFx_Mcm_<PropertyName>_Hint`; MCM group `PFx_McmGroup_<ConstName>`.
  Ids are never reused for a different text.
- **MCM groups**: MCM localizes each `|` segment on its own, so each segment carries its own id:
  `Battle + "|{=PFx_McmGroup_MovementSpeed}Movement speed"`. `DisplayName` is not localized by MCM;
  return `new TextObject("{=PFx_Mcm_ModName}...").ToString()`.
- **Whole sentences only**: never build a sentence with `+` from pieces at runtime (other languages
  need a different word order). Write one complete string per variant. Compile-time constants such
  as `+ LoadNote` are fine: they fold into one string with one id.
- **Numbers go in variables**: no `$"..."` interpolation in descriptions. Use `{VALUE}` (filled by the
  game from the perk bonus) or your own `{NAME}` set with `SetTextVariable`
  (see `SetMinisterHitpoints` in `PerkChanges.cs`).
- **Update the template in the same commit**: add, change or remove the matching
  `<string id="..." text="..." />` in `ModuleData/Languages/pfx_strings_en.xml` (line breaks as `&#10;`,
  quotes as `&quot;`). When English text changes, keep its id and change the text in both places.
- **Check before committing**: `powershell -File tools/check-localization.ps1` must print
  `Localization OK`. It lists untagged strings, ids missing from or stale in the template, and text
  that differs from the code.
- **Other language folders** under `ModuleData/Languages/` belong to translators. Don't edit them.
- **Release zips include `ModuleData/`** next to `bin/` and `SubModule.xml`.
